    "revision": "3237930758c228d1669fe1b9092e8a855b2c6b52",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "findings": [
      {
        "severity": "minor",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/tests/helpers/provider-guard.mjs",
        "line": 103,
        "claim": "The runner deletes the shim directory on exit, so a supervisor daemon that a test leaked resolves claude to the real CLI on its next tick after the run ends.",
        "evidence": "The exit handler runs rmSync(dir, {recursive:true}) while the leaked daemon's PATH still starts with that now-missing directory. PATH lookup then falls through to the operator's real provider CLI. Leaked supervise daemons are the failure this task defends against, and the CHANGELOG headline says 'No test can start a real provider CLI'.",
        "fix": "Leave the shims in place (a stable per-user directory, or skip the rmSync), or have the exit handler also fail the run when any supervise process for a temp repo is still alive. Otherwise narrow the CHANGELOG claim to spawns during the run."
      },
      {
        "severity": "nit",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/CHANGELOG.md",
        "line": 14,
        "claim": "The CHANGELOG says 'the test file that ran it fails', but the guard fails the whole run and only names the file; the test file's own result does not change.",
        "evidence": "provider-guard.mjs sets process.exitCode = 1 in the runner's exit handler and writes the file name to stderr; nothing marks the individual test as failed.",
        "fix": "Reword to: the run exits non-zero and names the test file that spawned the provider."
      },
      {
        "severity": "note",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/tests/helpers/provider-guard.mjs",
        "line": 95,
        "claim": "The guard only catches spawns that look up a bare command name on PATH. A test that sets PATH explicitly without the shim directory, or a provider configured by absolute path, gets past it."
      },
      {
        "severity": "note",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/CHANGELOG.md",
        "line": 17,
        "claim": "The request includes no test-run output, so the claim that the guard found six spawns in four files, and that the suite now passes with the guard on, is unverified. This approval rests on reading the diff, not on any check result."
      }
    ],
